# Valgrind memcheck suppression file for the Cell 8 curated subset.
#
# Policy: only third-party / test-harness allocations whose lifetime is
# pinned to the process by design may be suppressed. Any "possibly lost"
# or "definitely lost" entry whose stack contains a frame from
# `src/lockfree/...` or `src/debra/...` is a release blocker and must NOT
# be suppressed.
#
# Each entry MUST be annotated with:
#   - The exact stack frames (`fun:<symbol>`)
#   - A one-line justification
#   - A category tag: pre-existing-test-harness, pre-existing-nim-runtime,
#     or false-positive
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Suppressions below this line:

# Category: pre-existing-test-harness
# Justification: unittest2's ConsoleOutputFormatter is allocated at
# PreMain (NimMain) and intentionally lives for the lifetime of the
# process — there is no shutdown hook that frees it. Valgrind reports
# "possibly lost: 168 bytes" because the only references live in a
# thread-local stash that PreMain unwinds before exit. This is a
# property of the upstream unittest2 framework, not our code; no Nim or
# lockfree frame appears in the stack.
{
   unittest2-console-formatter-premain
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:malloc
   fun:*allocImpl*
   fun:*allocSharedImpl*
   fun:*alignedAlloc*
   fun:*alignedAlloc0*
   fun:nimNewObj
   fun:*newConsoleOutputFormatter*
   fun:*parseParameters*
   fun:*ensureInitialized*
   ...
}
